# ROM files.
#
# NOTE: .sfc / .smc are intentionally NOT ignored. The repo owner has chosen to
# commit the ROM (e.g. assets/Super Mario All-Stars (USA).sfc) directly via the
# GitHub web UI so it deploys with the app to Netlify, and is accepting the
# associated risk WHILE THE REPOSITORY IS PRIVATE.
#
# WARNING: committing a ROM writes it into git history permanently. If this repo
# is ever made PUBLIC, every historical commit that contains the ROM becomes
# public too, and removing it later requires a destructive history rewrite
# (force-push). Keep this repo private for as long as the ROM is committed.
#
# .zip stays ignored to avoid accidentally committing large/unrelated archives;
# it does not affect committing a raw .sfc/.smc ROM.
assets/*.zip

# NOTE: the from-source bsnes-mercury WASM cores (ASYNCIFY builds of both the
# accuracy AND performance profiles — cores/bsnes_mercury_accuracy_libretro.js +
# .wasm and cores/bsnes_mercury_performance_libretro.js + .wasm, plus core.json,
# build.json, license.txt) are bundled and TRACKED so they deploy with the app
# shell to Netlify. They are not ignored here on purpose.

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
node_modules/

# Emulator save-state blobs written by tools/hud-calibrate.mjs as a local
# reproducibility cache. These are the harness's OWN serialized emulator state
# (RAM/registers), not the ROM, but they are large binary artifacts and MUST NOT
# be committed. Regenerated on demand by running the harness.
*.state
